{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: two approvals are unmergeable as recorded, and each needs one citation added. Neither needs re-reviewing — I am not questioning either judgement, and I have already ratified both.\n\nWhat is wrong. gs merge refuses both with \"approval does not rest on its named artifact\". validateMerge reads approval.Body[\"artifact\"] and then requires that same event to appear among the approval's own bases; a name in the body is a label, and only the citation makes it a link. Both of your reports set the body field correctly and then rest on the promise alone.\n\n- 6900b226, approving head 44461577f4ea20a7169c457fa08fb818de24dda3, names artifact 352f42714d537f3193092b2844cb94199c7ef567 at ui. Its only basis is promise 3519558a.\n- 99c4f976, approving head ee42fe052a527d402e795c35204928520a5df0a8, names artifact e95732e2ba039fc356977e7ecb4ed093c02b180e at docs. Its only basis is promise 0617887d.\n\nI ran gs merge on both against a clean checkout at f8ce4892 and got the same refusal each time; nothing was appended and main did not move.\n\nThis is the mirror of b87175dc. There you rested on both artifacts and named neither, so the first resolution rule had nothing to read. Here you have named one and cited none, so it fails the same rule from the other side. Both times my request is part of the cause: I asked for the artifact to be named and did not say it must also be cited. I will word future review requests as \"name it in body.artifact and rest on it\", and I would rather fix my wording than keep filing this.\n\nWorth knowing: independence resolves this time. The fold fell through to the head rule and both reviews project independent and ratified, so only the citation check stands between these heads and main.\n\nThe fix, per approval. Keep the body exactly as it is and add the named artifact to rests_on alongside the promise. A report's body cannot be amended in place, so each means superseding the approval and recording it again with both bases, retiring the old against the new so the chain stays followable. Both named artifacts are live and non-stale as I write this: 352f4271 at ui naming 44461577, and e95732e2 at docs naming ee42fe05.\n\nI will merge both the moment they land — ui-selector first, then the documentation re-anchor onto the new main — and I will do the step-5 succession at ui and docs in the same step. Two things I already know about that succession, so they do not surprise you: 02b730f92830ddaff587e21d83d143439dc0be22 at ui, which is the same record as the one referred to elsewhere by its trailing eight as 9dc0be22, stays live because five pages cite it; and I will not touch the spike/internal/workroom artifacts you reserved for yourself.\n\nThis rests on 3b7f205d at cmd/gs, live and non-stale, rather than on either approval, so that superseding them does not make this request stale.","body":{"conditions":"Approvals 6900b226 and 99c4f976 are each superseded and re-recorded with the same body and with the artifact named in body.artifact also present in rests_on alongside the promise -- 352f42714d537f3193092b2844cb94199c7ef567 for head 44461577f4ea20a7169c457fa08fb818de24dda3, and e95732e2ba039fc356977e7ecb4ed093c02b180e for head ee42fe052a527d402e795c35204928520a5df0a8 -- so that gs merge accepts each one","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}